The installing routines are straightforward: all the necessary instructions
are presented on the screen, as required. The DOS program XCOPY must be in
the path. Enter may be pressed to end the installation during disk
operations: Ctrl-C or Ctrl-Break ends the installation when input is required.
   The routines automatically overwrite existing files with the same names.
This warning will be repeated later.
	It was not possible to make the presentation on the screen both
elegant and uncluttered, and to retain the trapping of errors. Consequently,
the routines do not stop if the destination disk becomes full: nor is any
error message presented. No harm other than wasted time will result.
	Before installing each set of files and after each file is installed,
the number of bytes remaining on the disk is shown (approximately, especially
if disk compression is used). For a complete installation, 8 megabytes of
hard disk space are required: it is the user's responsibility to ensure that
this space is available. The user may install 1) the chapters of the book (1
megabyte), 2) the programs (500k), 3) the ms data (1.7 megabytes), 4) the
chant files (5.2 megabytes), or 5) the miscellaneous files (100k) or any
combination of those five categories.  In addition, many
files may be uncompressed individually, by using the program PKUNZIP
(licensed from PKWARE). This program is on the root directory of disk 1, and
is copied to drive c: in the first stages of installing. The command is
followed by the drive, path, and filename and the drive to which the file is
to be written:  PKUNZIP a:\book\chap-2-2 c:
	Press Enter to continue, or Ctrl-C to exit.
